   summary:"Álvarez grew up on his family's farm in Juanacatlán, Jalisco, where he learned to ride horses, and started boxing at about 13 after watching his older brother Rigoberto turn professional. He has been trained since boyhood by the father-and-son team Chepo and Eddy Reynoso, who turned him professional at 15 when they could not find junior opponents for him. He won world titles from light middleweight to light heavyweight and in 2021 became the first boxer to hold all four major super middleweight belts at once. His camps pair Reynoso's boxing work with a strength coach's programme, and for the 2023 Charlo fight he spent two months training at Lake Tahoe, around 1,800 m, away from his family.",
